The Small Grants Programme consists of the following stages: 


• 
announcement of the call for project proposals under the Small Grants 
Programme;  

• 
submission period for project proposals (three (3) weeks);  

• 
review and evaluation of project proposals (two (2) weeks);  

• 
announcement of results and notification of successful applicants (one (1) week);  

• 
execution of grant agreements (two (2) weeks);  

• 
implementation of projects by CSOs and monitoring by UNDP (ten (10) months);  

• 
completion of project activities and submission of final implementation reports 
(within two (2) weeks following completion of the grant agreement). 

The deadline for submission of project proposals is 31 August 2026. 
Project proposals shall be received by the Implementing Organization. Applications must 
be submitted electronically to gulnoza.akhmedova@undp.org. 


VI. Budget 

6.1. The total budget of the Small Grants Programme for 2026–2027 amounts to USD 
40,000. In accordance with UNDP rules and procedures, the maximum amount that may 
be requested under a single project proposal shall not exceed USD 8 000, payable in the 
national currency at the UNDP exchange rate applicable on the date of submission. It is 
anticipated that five (5) grants will be awarded. 

